# Ymir commit message template
# Opt in locally: git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Format:
#   <type>(<scope>): <TASK-ID> - <one-line summary>
#
#   <2-4 line body explaining what landed, what tests ship, any gotchas>
#
#   Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>   # if AI-assisted
#
# ─── Types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat      New feature or capability
#   fix       Bug fix
#   docs      Documentation only
#   refactor  Code change that is not a feature or fix
#   perf      Performance improvement
#   test      Adding or correcting tests
#   build     Build system / Cargo.toml / dependency changes
#   ci        CI/CD workflow changes
#   chore     Everything else (tooling, config, maintenance)
#
# ─── Scopes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   core | catalog | system | atmosphere | surface | climate | biome |
#   detail | render | storage    (crate name without the ymir- prefix)
#   ymir        the binary crate at the repo root
#   workspace   cross-cutting changes (multiple crates or repo-level config)
#
# ─── Breaking changes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Append ! before the colon: feat(core)!: CORE-12 - rename Sourced trait
#   release-plz uses this to bump the minor version (pre-1.0) or major (post-1.0).
#
# ─── Examples ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat(detail): REGN-06 - HexGrid subdivision
#   fix(climate): CLIM-03 - clamp albedo at poles
#   docs(workspace): INFRA-11 - adopt conventional-commits prefix
#   ci(workspace): INFRA-09 - wire release-plz workflow
#
